{
  "_comment": "EIP-712 array-of-struct hashing regression + parity references. messageHash is the EIP-712 hashStruct(message) digest, computed independently by @metamask/eth-sig-util V4 and ethers v6 (they agree). The Ledger device must hash to the same value or eth_account.recover_message in test_eip712.py recovers a different signer and the device test fails. triggers: bugA = element struct encoding hits the 136-byte keccak rate boundary (single-level OR directly-nested, depth>0); bugB = nested fixed custom-struct array depth>=2; classC = empty dynamic array immediately before a custom-struct field (scalar- or struct-element array); classR-regguard = array element whose first field is a nested struct (must hash correctly on BOTH develop and fixed: guards that the Bug-B fix did not regress struct-first elements); gapA = nested array (depth>=2, fixed or dynamic) whose element struct's FIRST field is itself a custom struct (intersection of the Bug-B nested-array splice and the Class-R struct-first element handling at inner array levels); gapB = empty custom-struct array occupying an inner dimension of a multi-dimensional struct array (e.g. Leaf[][] with x=[[]]); none-parity = bundled eth-sig-util/ethers per-type parity matrix; none-control = unaffected reference. The gapA/gapB shapes were previously carved out under KNOWN LIMITATIONS and are now fixed (they DIVERGE on pristine develop and MATCH on the fixed source). See src/features/sign_message_eip712/path.c.",
